`EXCHANGE_DLP` and `DEFENDER_XDR` are Maester's own tokens for a group of plans; every other token in the table
is the service plan's own name.

Any other token is compared literally with the tenant's service plan names, so a custom test can use any plan
name.

For the tests shipped with Maester this is checked. The unit test "Names a service plan in License, not a
product" in `powershell/tests/general/NativeTestAttributes.Tests.ps1` fails when a `License` value is neither a
name from Microsoft's Service plans included column nor a token of `powershell/assets/MaesterLicenseTable.psd1`.
The list of Microsoft's names is `website/src/data/license-service-plans.json`, which a scheduled workflow
refreshes from the Microsoft page every day. Only enabled subscriptions count. When the licences cannot be read (no Graph connection, or no
permission), the licence check is not applied and the test runs.

### Permission

`Permission` says what the identity Maester signs in with must be granted for the test to read its data. It
is recorded on the result row and in the catalog, so the docs and the report can say what to grant; Maester 3.0
does not skip a test on it.

Each permission is written `<Service>:<Kind>:<Name>`:

